Chapter: RoyalUrWasm
  cites Games chapter RoyalUr
  cites Games chapter Rng
  cites Foreword chapter List

 The browser interface for the Royal Game of Ur. TicTacToe threads its whole
 state through the page as one base-4 integer; Ur cannot, because seven
 pieces a side at four bits each plus the flags is about 71 bits and the
 export wrapper narrows to a signed i32. The page therefore holds a HANDLE:
 a record is a heap object, so the reference the wrapper narrows already is
 the board's address, and the page hands it back on the next call.

 A handle is a VALUE here, not a cursor into a board that moves underneath
 it. That takes one deliberate copy. `list-set-at` mutates in place and
 returns the same list, so `ur-apply-move` writes through to the lists of
 the board it was handed; without the copy below, playing from a handle
 would leave the caller's own board holding the move, with its scalar
 fields still reading the position before it. `ttt-copy-squares` in
 TicTacToe is the same idiom for the same reason.

 The dice are the page's, not ours. `ur-wasm-roll` takes a seed and answers
 the four-binary-dice total for it, so a transcript of seeds replays a game
 exactly and the grader can assert against a fixed one.

 We say:

Section: Copying

  ur-copy-pieces : List Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  ur-copy-pieces (src) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= 7 then acc
    else ur-copy-pieces src (i + 1) (list-push acc (list-at src i))

  ur-copy-board : UrBoard -> UrBoard
  ur-copy-board (b) =
    UrBoard {
      p1-pieces = ur-copy-pieces (b.p1-pieces) 0 [],
      p2-pieces = ur-copy-pieces (b.p2-pieces) 0 [],
      current-player = b.current-player,
      p1-scored = b.p1-scored,
      p2-scored = b.p2-scored,
      game-over = b.game-over,
      winner = b.winner,
      last-roll = b.last-roll,
      moves-made = b.moves-made
    }

Section: The Browser Interface

  ur-wasm-new : UrBoard
  ur-wasm-new = ur-new

  ur-wasm-roll : Integer -> Integer
  ur-wasm-roll (seed) = ur-roll (rng-new seed)

  ur-wasm-play : UrBoard, Integer, Integer -> UrBoard
  ur-wasm-play (b) (idx) (roll) =
    if ur-wasm-can b idx roll == 0 then b
    else ur-apply-move (ur-copy-board b) idx roll

  ur-wasm-can : UrBoard, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  ur-wasm-can (b) (idx) (roll) =
    if b.game-over then 0
    else if idx < 0 then 0
    else if idx >= 7 then 0
    else if roll <= 0 then 0
    else if roll > 4 then 0
    else let mine = if b.current-player == 1 then b.p1-pieces else b.p2-pieces
    in let theirs = if b.current-player == 1 then b.p2-pieces else b.p1-pieces
    in let step = list-at mine idx
    in let target = step + roll
    in if step == 15 then 0
    else if target > 15 then 0
    else if target /= 15 & ur-piece-at-step mine target then 0
    else if ur-is-shared target & ur-piece-at-step theirs target & ur-is-rosette target then 0
    else 1

  ur-wasm-pass : UrBoard -> UrBoard
  ur-wasm-pass (b) =
    if b.game-over then b
    else UrBoard {
      p1-pieces = ur-copy-pieces (b.p1-pieces) 0 [],
      p2-pieces = ur-copy-pieces (b.p2-pieces) 0 [],
      current-player = if b.current-player == 1 then 2 else 1,
      p1-scored = b.p1-scored,
      p2-scored = b.p2-scored,
      game-over = b.game-over,
      winner = b.winner,
      last-roll = 0,
      moves-made = b.moves-made + 1
    }

  ur-wasm-ai : UrBoard, Integer -> Integer
  ur-wasm-ai (b) (roll) =
    if b.game-over then (-1)
    else if roll <= 0 then (-1)
    else ur-ai-pick b roll

  ur-wasm-piece : UrBoard, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  ur-wasm-piece (b) (player) (i) =
    if i < 0 then (-1)
    else if i >= 7 then (-1)
    else if player == 1 then list-at (b.p1-pieces) i
    else list-at (b.p2-pieces) i

  ur-wasm-cur : UrBoard -> Integer
  ur-wasm-cur (b) = b.current-player

  ur-wasm-scored : UrBoard, Integer -> Integer
  ur-wasm-scored (b) (player) =
    if player == 1 then b.p1-scored else b.p2-scored

  ur-wasm-done : UrBoard -> Integer
  ur-wasm-done (b) = if b.game-over then 1 else 0

  ur-wasm-winner : UrBoard -> Integer
  ur-wasm-winner (b) = b.winner

  ur-wasm-moves : UrBoard -> Integer
  ur-wasm-moves (b) = b.moves-made

